WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.140
The first epic trailer for the Captain Underpants
movie just dropped and as it's based on the

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.490
best-selling book series, the movie looks
like it will be packed with easter eggs and

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.070
references to the original novels by Dav Pilkey.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.839
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video, I'll be revealing some

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:18.680
cool easter eggs and other interesting details
you might have missed in the first full Captain

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.380
Underpants movie trailer.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.980
So let's start with pranksters George and
Harold are creating comics in a treehouse,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.180
and you'll see that in the middle of the floor
is the brand name they use for their comics,

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.300
"Treehouse Comix Inc".

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.940
There's also a Robo-Boogers easter egg on
one of the comic book covers we see in the

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:33.940
treehouse.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.559
The Robo-Boogers are monsters which appear
in the "Bionic Booger Boy" books of the Captain

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:41.809
Underpants series and, as you might expect
from their name, they are technological creations

00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:43.629
based on snot.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:47.359
And there's another clever hint to the Robo-Boogers
later in the trailer via the Snotco sign on

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:49.679
the building that Captain Underpants runs
along.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:53.980
Ok, let's get to Captain Underpants himself
as the trailer reveals how George and Harold

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.229
transform their mean Principal Krupp.

00:00:56.229 --> 00:01:00.460
George uses a Hypno Ring to hypnotise Krupp
and make him think he's the Captain Underpants

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.210
character from their comic books.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.061
This transformation is similar to the first
Captain Underpants book where George and Harold

00:01:06.061 --> 00:01:10.160
use a Hypno Ring to hypnotise Krupp when they
want to recover a videotape the principal

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.990
is using to blackmail them into performing
chores for him.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.380
In the movie though, it looks like George
and Harold use it to stop Krupp putting them

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.780
in separate classes.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.670
After Krupp's been hypnotised, George snaps
his fingers presumably because he thinks this

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.590
will snap Krupp out of his state.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.290
However the snap kicks off Krupp's transformation.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:30.500
In the books, whenever someone snaps their
fingers, Krupp automatically turns into Captain

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.530
Underpants.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:36.289
And in the trailer, after his transformation,
he delivers his classic catchphrase, "Tra-la-laaa!"

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:40.729
Mr Krupp aka Captain Underpants is voiced
by actor Ed Helms, who was one of the stars

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:41.869
of The Hangover movies.

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:46.630
So, I wonder if George and Harold's prank
with the tiger could be a hint to the first

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.850
Hangover movie where Ed Helms sings a song
about a tiger that appears as part of a prank

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.310
in his hotel room in Las Vegas.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.790
While Captain Underpants is battling a giant
inflatable ape, in the city skyline you can

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:01.960
see a billboard for "John's House of Toilets",
a building which appears in Part 2 of the

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.600
"Bionic Booger Boy" books.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.859
In that story, Captain Underpants stands on
top of "John's House of Toilets" where he

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:11.560
performs the Underpants dance to annoy and
bait the Robo-Boogers.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.700
Next up in the trailer, we get to meet Professor
P, who stresses, rather amusingly, that he's

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.680
not the evil villain of the story.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.920
Professor P's full name is "Professor Pippy
Pee-Pee Poopypants" and the character was

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.680
introduced in the fourth Captain Underpants
book.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:28.480
And if you feel like you recognise Professor
P's voice from another recent animation, that's

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.260
because it's Nick Kroll, the voice of the
all-singing, all-dancing pig Gunter in the

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.090
animated movie, Sing.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.720
And Professor P is clearly controlling this
giant toilet character who is likely Turbo

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.599
Toilet 2000, the leader of The Talking Toilets
from the second Captain Underpants book "Attack

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:45.260
of the Talking Toilets".

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.340
Talking of toilets, it looks like George and
Harold played a prank on classmate Melvin

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.519
while he's demonstrating some kind of toilet
invention.

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.489
Melvin's toilet invention is clearly going
haywire and this might be the prank which

00:02:56.489 --> 00:03:00.170
got George and Harold into so much trouble
with principal Krupp.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.720
Melvin is the nemesis of George and Harold
in the "Attack of the Talking Toilets" book

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:09.060
where he invents the PATSY 2000, a photocopier
that can convert any 2D-image into a real

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.060
object.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.580
And in this other shot, it looks like Melvin
is teaming up with the nefarious Professor

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.900
P.
Interestingly, in "Attack of the Talking Toilets",

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.040
it was Melvin's PATSY 2000 invention which
was responsible for the creation of the Talking

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.660
Toilets, so I wonder if, in this movie, Melvin
and Professor P will be the ones responsible

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.799
for creating Turbo Toilet?

00:03:27.799 --> 00:03:31.549
When Captain Underpants takes out two bank
robbers at Frank's Bank, it's a nod to the

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:35.520
very first crime he stopped in the first novel,
although in that book it's because the robbers

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.020
couldn't stop laughing after he told them
to surrender or he'd use "wedgie power" on

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.020
them!

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.870
And finally, did you spot the amusing store
called "Everything Except Fabric Softener:

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.990
The Store For All Your Non-Fabric Softening
Needs"?!

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:51.630
Well, it's a location that appears in a number
of the novels and, as the name suggests, it

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.060
sells almost everything, but definitely not
fabric softener!

00:03:55.060 --> 00:04:00.000
So, what did you think of the first Captain
Underpants trailer?!

